  "id": "Compound::DB00177 - Gene::28234",
  "verbalization": "Valsartan, a member of the angiotensin II receptor antagonists, is linked to Slco1b3 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Valsartan, as part of the broader class of angiotensin II receptor antagonists, binds to Slco1b3, a transporter involved in the uptake of certain compounds. This relationship is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) of Valsartan and Telmisartan, which points to the Angiotensin II Receptor Antagonist category, and the subsequent binding to Slco1b3. Similarly, Valsartan's resemblance to Forasartan and Olmesartan, which also bind to Slco1b3, further reinforces the connection. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where angiotensin II receptor antagonists, through their structural similarities and shared binding sites, influence the activity of Slco1b3. The evidence suggests a direct or indirect interaction between Valsartan and Slco1b3, mediated through the angiotensin II receptor antagonists' pharmacological profile.",
